<section id="qa"><h2>6. Guide questions</h2>
<div class="qa"><h3>How long have you been studying Systems Engineering?</h3><p>I have been studying Systems Engineering at Universidad del Pacífico for several semesters, focusing on software architecture, web development, and database management.</p></div>
<div class="qa"><h3>What programming language have you been learning recently?</h3><p>Lately, I have been learning advanced Python features, utilizing Flask frameworks, and structuring relational queries with MySQL for our software projects.</p></div>
<div class="qa"><h3>What project have you been working on for a long time?</h3><p>For the past few months, my team and I have been working intensively on SICUA (Sistema Inteligente de Control de Acceso Universitario), automating entry controls for students, teachers, and administrators.</p></div>
<div class="qa"><h3>What problem have you been trying to solve?</h3><p>We have been trying to solve the lack of digital traceability and security vulnerabilities at the university's main entrance, where traditional unrecorded manual access creates risks of unauthorized entries.</p></div>
