<section id="talk"><h2>7. Oral presentation: “My Dev Journey”</h2>
<p>Three minutes, shared between both of us. <b>1</b> and <b>2</b> take turns.</p>
<ul class="talk">
<li><span class="who w1">1</span>Good morning, teacher and classmates. I'm Sarly Naranjo.</li>
<li><span class="who w2">2</span>And I'm Emmanuel Paz. Today we are going to talk about our journey in Systems Engineering.</li>
<li><span class="who w1">1</span>We have been studying Systems Engineering at Universidad del Pacífico for several semesters, focusing on software and databases.</li>
<li><span class="who w2">2</span>Lately, we have been learning advanced Python features, using Flask, and writing queries with MySQL.</li>
<li><span class="who w1">1</span>For the past few months, our team has been working on SICUA, a web platform that controls access to our university.</li>
<li><span class="who w2">2</span>We have been trying to solve the lack of digital traceability at the main entrance.</li>
<li><span class="who w1">1</span>We have been designing the database and building a login for each user role.</li>
<li><span class="who w2">2</span>We have been testing the guard interface recently, where the guard validates digital access codes.</li>
<li><span class="who w1">1</span>We have been learning technical vocabulary like debugging, authenticating, validating, and securing.</li>
<li><span class="who w2">2</span>We have been upgrading our prototype toward a dynamic QR code, and we have been documenting every step.</li>
<li><span class="who w1">1</span>We have been learning that building software requires practice, patience, and teamwork.</li>
<li><span class="who w2">2</span>Finally, we have been preparing ourselves for international teams and technical interviews. Thank you for listening!</li>
</ul>
